.TH MANTA-CERT 1 "manta-cert v1.0.0" "Manta Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
manta-cert \- check SSL/TLS certificate expiry dates for domains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cert [options] <domain...>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check the expiry date of SSL/TLS certificates for one or more domains. Shows days remaining and warns when a certificate is expired or close to expiry. Zero external dependencies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B domain...
One or more domain names to check
.TP
.B -p, --port PORT
TCP port to connect to (default: 443)
.TP
.B -w, --warn DAYS
Warning threshold in days (default: 30)
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Show full certificate details
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Connection timeout (default: 10)
.TP
.B --version
Show version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check a domain
.B cert example.com
.TP
Check multiple domains
.B cert example.com google.com github.com
.TP
Custom port
.B cert example.com --port 8443
.TP
14-day warning threshold
.B cert example.com --warn 14
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
All certificates valid and within warning threshold
.TP
.B 1
Certificate expired or connection error
